WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.048 --> 00:00:16.176
The next day I awoke after sleeping for twelve hours.

2
00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:20.279
As usual Conseil came to my room to see if I needed anything.

3
00:00:20.299 --> 00:00:22.000
"Did you sleep well?"

4
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.462
he asked as he did every day when we were living on land.

5
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:27.704
"Quite well," I replied.

6
00:00:27.724 --> 00:00:28.825
"Where's Ned?"

7
00:00:28.845 --> 00:00:30.726
"Still sleeping, Master.

8
00:00:31.086 --> 00:00:33.448
Ned appears to have plenty of practice at sleeping.

9
00:00:33.792 --> 00:00:39.775
He sleeps so soundly that I Conseil chattered on, but I didn't respond because I was thinking about

10
00:00:39.816 --> 00:00:40.536
Captain Nemo.

11
00:00:41.516 --> 00:00:42.977
Why hadn't we seen him last night?

12
00:00:43.638 --> 00:00:45.219
I was sure he'd make an appearance today.

13
00:00:46.159 --> 00:00:48.480
As soon as I was dressed, I went into the gallery.

14
00:00:49.241 --> 00:00:49.901
It was deserted.

15
00:00:50.642 --> 00:00:53.203
I plunged into studying the shells in the glass cases.

16
00:00:54.144 --> 00:00:57.445
I also enjoyed the huge albums filled with rare marine plants.

17
00:00:58.386 --> 00:01:01.568
Even though the plants were dried, they retained their lovely colors.

18
00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.901
The whole day passed without Captain Nemo honoring me with a visit.

19
00:01:06.841 --> 00:01:08.902
The panels in the museum room did not open.

20
00:01:09.582 --> 00:01:12.203
Perhaps he did not wish us to tire of the beautiful view.

21
00:01:13.183 --> 00:01:19.065
The Nautilus continued on its course, traveling at a depth ranging from 150 to 180 feet.

22
00:01:20.025 --> 00:01:24.146
The next day, November 10, I didn't see a single member of the ship's crew.

23
00:01:25.186 --> 00:01:30.628
Ned and Conseil spent most of the day with me, and they were astonished at the inexplicable absence

24
00:01:30.668 --> 00:01:31.188
of the captain.

25
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.882
Was this eccentric man ill?

26
00:01:34.562 --> 00:01:37.245
Had he changed his mind about how he was going to treat us?

27
00:01:38.325 --> 00:01:44.671
But as Conseil pointed out, we were still free to roam the submarine and we were always provided

28
00:01:44.691 --> 00:01:46.432
with delicious and abundant food.

29
00:01:47.453 --> 00:01:52.558
Our host kept his part of the bargain, and we couldn't complain because this voyage really was a

30
00:01:52.758 --> 00:01:54.159
once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

31
00:01:55.600 --> 00:02:01.337
Early the next morning, November 11, I could smell fresh sea air, so I knew that the Nautilus

32
00:02:01.357 --> 00:02:02.418
had risen to the surface.

33
00:02:03.419 --> 00:02:07.102
I went up on the platform, where I fully expected to meet Captain Nemo.

34
00:02:08.023 --> 00:02:12.527
It was six o'clock; the sky was cloudy and the sea was gray but calm.

35
00:02:13.487 --> 00:02:16.150
I saw no one except the pilot in his glass cage.

36
00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:22.215
I inhaled the salt air with delight as the sun's rays gradually burned away the fog.

37
00:02:23.156 --> 00:02:26.899
I was admiring the sunrise when I heard someone climbing up to the platform.

38
00:02:27.759 --> 00:02:30.509
I turned, fully expecting to greet Captain Nemo.

39
00:02:31.349 --> 00:02:36.011
But it was only his second-in-command, his lieutenant, the other man that I'd met on our first day

40
00:02:36.251 --> 00:02:37.112
onboard the Nautilus.

41
00:02:38.032 --> 00:02:40.253
He climbed onto the platform without seeming to see me.

42
00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:45.295
Putting his telescope to his eye, he scanned the horizon with great attention.

43
00:02:46.276 --> 00:02:51.798
When he'd finished, he went to the hatch and called down, "Nautron respoc lorni virch."

44
00:02:53.359 --> 00:02:58.937
What these words meant I couldn't say, but I have remembered this sentence because he repeated it every

45
00:02:59.018 --> 00:03:01.278
day under the exact same conditions.

46
00:03:02.279 --> 00:03:05.800
Having uttered these words, Nemo's lieutenant descended through the hatch.

47
00:03:06.781 --> 00:03:11.143
I thought that the Nautilus was about to resume its underwater voyage, so I went down to my

48
00:03:11.183 --> 00:03:16.105
cabin. Five days passed like this without any change in our situation.

49
00:03:16.965 --> 00:03:18.906
Every morning I mounted the platform.

50
00:03:19.826 --> 00:03:23.348
The same man said the same sentence in the same strange language.

51
00:03:24.064 --> 00:03:25.645
Captain Nemo did not appear.

52
00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.867
I had made up my mind that I would never see him again.

53
00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:35.212
But on November 16, I returned to my cabin with Ned and Conseil and found an envelope on

54
00:03:35.252 --> 00:03:35.752
my table.

55
00:03:36.693 --> 00:03:40.896
I opened it impatiently and read a note in bold, clear handwriting.

56
00:03:42.317 --> 00:03:50.273
The note was worded as follows: To Professor Aronnax onboard the Nautilus: Captain Nemo invites Professor Aronnax to

57
00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:55.736
a hunting party that will take place tomorrow morning in his forests on the island of Crespo.

58
00:03:56.617 --> 00:03:59.638
The captain hopes that nothing will prevent the professor from being present.

59
00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:03.521
The professor's companions are also invited to join the hunt.

60
00:04:04.301 --> 00:04:08.083
Captain Nemo, commander of the Nautilus "A hunt!"

61
00:04:08.523 --> 00:04:09.204
exclaimed Ned.

62
00:04:09.224 --> 00:04:13.166
"And in his forests on the island of Crespo!"

63
00:04:13.526 --> 00:04:14.206
added Conseil.

64
00:04:14.226 --> 00:04:17.932
"So it sounds like the captain is going ashore," said Ned.

65
00:04:18.873 --> 00:04:19.774
I read the note again.

66
00:04:19.794 --> 00:04:23.516
"It certainly does seem that way," I said.

67
00:04:24.477 --> 00:04:27.719
"Well, we must definitely accept this invitation," said Ned.

68
00:04:27.739 --> 00:04:32.102
"All this fish is fine, but I wouldn't mind eating some fresh venison."

69
00:04:33.103 --> 00:04:35.765
I was still trying to make sense of Captain Nemo's invitation.

70
00:04:36.665 --> 00:04:41.268
He planned to go hunting in a forest yet had a strong aversion to anything on land.

71
00:04:42.189 --> 00:04:44.351
"I've never heard of this island," I said.

72
00:04:44.371 --> 00:04:46.112
"Let's find out where it is."

73
00:04:47.092 --> 00:04:52.316
I consulted the map and showed my companions a tiny island lost in the middle of the northern

74
00:04:52.336 --> 00:04:57.179
Pacific. I also noted that we were about 800 leagues from our starting point.

75
00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.644
"If Captain Nemo sometimes does go on dry land," I said, "he certainly chooses remote islands."

76
00:05:04.564 --> 00:05:07.786
The rest of the day passed without another word or visit from the captain.

77
00:05:09.327 --> 00:05:13.710
When I awoke the next morning, I could feel that the Nautilus was perfectly still.

78
00:05:14.671 --> 00:05:18.598
I dressed quickly and entered the gallery, where I found Captain Nemo.

79
00:05:19.598 --> 00:05:24.921
He made no reference to his absence for the past eight days, but simply asked if we would

80
00:05:24.981 --> 00:05:26.302
be accompanying him today.

81
00:05:26.322 --> 00:05:28.643
"We will," I replied.

82
00:05:28.663 --> 00:05:35.307
"But I'm puzzled by one thing: How can you own forests on Crespo Island if you've cut all

83
00:05:35.347 --> 00:05:36.348
ties with land?"

84
00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:41.291
"My forests don't bask in the heat and light of the sun," he replied.

85
00:05:41.311 --> 00:05:45.970
"They aren't on land; they're actual underwater forests."

86
00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:49.932
"You're offering to take me to real underwater forests?"

87
00:05:50.713 --> 00:05:51.373
I couldn't believe it.

88
00:05:51.393 --> 00:05:54.815
"Yes, Professor, and without getting your feet wet.

89
00:05:55.556 --> 00:05:56.957
Now come eat breakfast with me.

90
00:05:57.978 --> 00:06:02.220
There aren't any restaurants on Crespo, and it will be a long time before you have supper."

91
00:06:03.661 --> 00:06:06.203
While we ate, I asked the captain some questions.

92
00:06:06.223 --> 00:06:12.167
"I'm familiar with a diving apparatus that lets a man breathe underwater, but he must stay tethered to

93
00:06:12.227 --> 00:06:13.408
a ship," I began.

94
00:06:14.492 --> 00:06:19.014
"Then there's a diving suit that allows a man to leave the ship, but it only contains a

95
00:06:19.074 --> 00:06:20.795
limited amount of air in a backpack.

96
00:06:21.675 --> 00:06:22.936
Which one will we be using?"

97
00:06:22.956 --> 00:06:26.417
"A version of the diving suit," said Captain Nemo.

98
00:06:26.437 --> 00:06:30.900
"I've improved it so that a man can stay underwater for nine or ten hours."

99
00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:34.181
"But how will we be able to see in the dark waters?

100
00:06:35.121 --> 00:06:37.382
And a regular gun won't fire in the water."

101
00:06:38.243 --> 00:06:39.043
The captain smiled.

102
00:06:39.063 --> 00:06:40.584
"Don't worry.

103
00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.921
I've invented both a light and a gun that will work underwater.

104
00:06:45.701 --> 00:06:46.782
Are you ready to go hunting?"

105
00:06:48.222 --> 00:06:52.483
We left the dining room and as we passed my companions' cabin, I called for them to join

106
00:06:52.523 --> 00:06:57.844
us. Near the engine room we came to a small room where we found a dozen diving suits.

107
00:06:59.305 --> 00:07:00.625
"Oh no," said Ned.

108
00:07:00.645 --> 00:07:02.886
"I'm not getting into one of those."

109
00:07:02.906 --> 00:07:05.967
"But there's no alternative," I said.

110
00:07:05.987 --> 00:07:08.847
"The forests of Crespo are underwater."

111
00:07:08.867 --> 00:07:14.771
"Underwater?" Ned seemed to realize that his dream of eating venison was slipping away.

112
00:07:14.791 --> 00:07:20.415
"Unless someone forces me, I won't be going with you," the harpooner replied firmly.

113
00:07:20.435 --> 00:07:22.936
"No one will force you, Mr.

114
00:07:22.976 --> 00:07:24.557
Land," said Captain Nemo.

115
00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:26.359
"Are you coming with us?"

116
00:07:26.859 --> 00:07:27.680
I asked Conseil.

117
00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:32.183
"I follow my master wherever he goes," replied my loyal servant.
